From: Roman Rikhter <teledurak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] jshn: keep key names when loading JSON

jshn -r writes every key of the loaded JSON with each character other
than a letter or a digit replaced by '_'. jshn.sh already maps such keys
to variable names itself and records the original name for json_dump,
but it never sees the original name of a loaded key. A JSON file that is
loaded and dumped again thus has "phy0-ap0" turned into "phy0_ap0", for
example in board.json, which every board.d script loads and writes back.

Write the key as it is, quoted for the single-quoted shell string.

Signed-off-by: Roman Rikhter <teledurak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/jshn.c
+++ b/jshn.c
@@ -94,7 +94,10 @@
 static void write_key_string(const char *key)
 {
 	while (*key) {
-		putc(isalnum(*key) ? *key : '_', stdout);
+		if (*key == '\'')
+			fputs("'\\''", stdout);
+		else
+			putc(*key, stdout);
 		key++;
 	}
 }
